   "recovered": "recovered: the location's hourly congestion component (settled sign) regressed on every binding constraint's hourly shadow price, least squares with an intercept, one fit per period (calendar year or run; never pooled). Contingency variants of one monitored facility are merged into one bar (their contributions summed). Bar = recovered shift factor × mean shadow price over every hour, $/MWh of the annual mean MCC. Gated (method.gates): location R² >= 0.95; facility >= 50 binding hours; VIF <= 10 on the merged design; κ <= 30; |bar| >= 0.01; |SF| <= 1. Each bar carries a ±max(0.01, 20 %) band: against exact DFAX at 317–332 PCR buses the gated facility bars pass that band 0.95 / 0.85 / 1.00 (pcr2030 / 2035 / 2040; constraint-level error p95 0.003–0.042, max 0.17 $/MWh). sf is the coefficient on the stored shadow price: its sign follows the store's convention (settled stored negative, PROBE positive), so only |sf| is physical — never colour by it.",
